# Upstream's .gitignore, two directories up, carries `reckless*` — meant for the
# built binary of that name. It also matches `include/reckless.h`, which is not
# upstream's and not built: it is the hand-written C header this app's bridge is
# made of, and without it `build-reckless.sh` stops at the copy and no
# xcframework is produced. Nothing then resolves the package, and Xcode reports
# it as a missing product, three steps from the cause.
#
# The rule lives here rather than beside the one it answers, because `bridge/` is
# ours and the directory above it is vendored: re-vendoring the engine would take
# a negation written up there away with it, and the header would go quiet again.
!include/reckless.h
